Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 16:54:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 72/77] ipc/sem: mark shared semaphore operation comment as
 non-kernel-doc

The comment documents both perform_atomic_semop() and its slow variant,
so it is not valid kernel-doc for the immediately following function.
Mark it as a regular block comment to prevent the documentation parser
from treating the bracketed name as an identifier.

No functional change.

Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5
---
 ipc/sem.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ipc/sem.c b/ipc/sem.c
index 6cdf862b1f5cc..89a003ac01660 100644
--- a/ipc/sem.c
+++ b/ipc/sem.c
@@ -626,7 +626,7 @@ SYSCALL_DEFINE3(semget, key_t, key, int, nsems, int, semflg)
 	return ksys_semget(key, nsems, semflg);
 }
 
-/**
+/*
  * perform_atomic_semop[_slow] - Attempt to perform semaphore
  *                               operations on a given array.
  * @sma: semaphore array
-- 
